# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""apply_esign_model.py - round ES-1, 23 Oct 2026.

E-SIGNING, RUNG ONE: THE THREE TABLES AND NOTHING ELSE.

No view, no screen, no email, no route. A model round that also
shipped a screen would be two claims in one, and when the sweep went
red neither half could say which.

AN ENVELOPE IS NOT A LEASE. None of this is a column on `tenant`.
`tenant.tenant_lease_agreement` stays exactly where it is as the place
a FINISHED lease lives; this is the ATTEMPT to get one signed, and an
attempt can expire, be cancelled, be resent, and be followed by
another attempt. A process stored on the thing it is about can only
ever have one of itself and has nowhere to put an audit trail.

THREE TABLES.

  LeaseSigning        one envelope - the document, its state, its
                      dates, and the sha256 of the sealed bytes
  LeaseSigningParty   one row per signer. One from Alivente and up to
                      two tenants, to two different addresses
  LeaseSigningEvent   append only. Created, sent, viewed, signed,
                      declined, sealed, delivered, expired, cancelled

THE AUDIT TRAIL IS THE EVIDENCE. There is no certificate - decided 23
October - so nothing in the FILE proves anything. This table and
pdf_sha256 are what a dispute is argued from, which is why nothing in
it is ever updated or deleted.

AND THE TOKEN IS STORED HASHED. The emailed link is the credential,
and a credential sitting readable in a database column is what
password resets stopped doing a decade ago. issue_token() returns the
raw token once, keeps sha256 of it, and nothing can read it back. A
resend mints a new one and the old link dies - which is also the only
honest behaviour, since a link that expires and then works again never
really expired.

UPLOADED ONLY. `source` exists now so the system-generated lease is a
branch in one view later rather than a migration and a second table.

A MIGRATION SHIPS WITH THIS ROUND. 0103, three CreateModel, no data
touched. Railway runs it on deploy.

Idempotent. Every file backed up to .bak_esignmodel.
"""
